{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791702990,"nonce":"OG94Tl58MhRZc+/kpPpbP20tCZ0=","title":"Table columns are equal shares, so wide content runs over the next cell","message":"Every column without a col width was minmax(0, 1fr): an equal share of the row, whatever its cells held. In the wiki's token table a column of code ran under the count beside it.\n\nColumns are now sized by their cells, as a browser's automatic table layout does. Every td and th is an inline flow, which knows the width its content takes on one line and its widest unbreakable piece (the flow sets them on its spacer). After the flows settle (InlineFlows.onSettled), Tables gives each sized column minmax(\u003cwidest min + inset\u003epx, \u003cwidest natural + inset\u003efr); beside columns given shares (col width=\"2*\"), a sized column takes minmax(min px, natural px) and leaves the rest to them. A cell spanning columns sizes none. The inset is the cell's padding and border, read as the spacer's offset in the cell and taken to be the same on both sides.\n\nSettling a table takes passes after the flows' own, so LAYOUT_PASSES went from 4 to 6: with 4, a narrow table's wrapped cell reached its height only on the next layout.\n\nTests: tests/native-tables.mjs checks columns line up, fill the row, size by content, a colspan spans, an unbreakable word holds its column open in a narrow table while the other wraps, settled in one layout; col widths in px, % and shares. Measuring disabled, it fails (\"a wider column for wider content\").","files":null}]}